WEBVTT

NOTE Original instrumental sound. Captions describe the fictional on-screen examples.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Eating Out is £240 against £120 usual by day 10. Overall spending is £860 against £740 usual.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
The four Eating Out payments are £92, £58, £48 and £42. They total £240.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Penny compares spending by category with usual spending at the same point in the pay period.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.000
Review a £600 car insurance plan: £200 on 30 November, 30 December and 30 January. Confirmation is required.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.000
After confirmation, the three payday contributions are scheduled in Sorted. No bank transfer is made.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.000
A £188 Energy payment has £68 in Bills. A suggested £80 from Everyday and £40 from Joint cover the £120 gap.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Sorted suggests the route. You decide, and make any transfer in your bank. Fictional examples throughout.

